---
description: Session-start enforcement gate (#54) — run the protocol, then acknowledge to unlock
alwaysApply: true
---

This workspace enforces the session-start protocol for Cursor via
`.cursor/hooks.json`. At the start of each session:

1. Run the session-start protocol (`agent/session-protocol.md` §0): load the
   layered context and **post the context manifest BEFORE changing code**.
2. As the **last step**, acknowledge to unlock edits + shell:

   ```bash
   bash .cursor/hooks/session-ack.sh
   ```

Until you acknowledge, file writes (`preToolUse`/`Write`) and shell
(`beforeShellExecution`) are denied by the hooks. (Layer-2 client gate; CI / merge
enforce the same uniformly at Layer 3.)
